module gunbc.plans.construction_justification_rule

import std.dissolution { unbound_dissolution }
import gunbc.plan { Plan, PlanRetirement, PlanRetiresWhen, PlanIsAuthorityOnly }
import std.markdown { MarkdownBlock }
import gunbc.plans.md_helpers { p }
import gunbc.design_ruling { project_documentation_projections_are_not_checkout_artifacts }

fn construction_justification_rule_body() -> List<MarkdownBlock> {
  [
    p(text: "Goal: use construction before validation; every proposed lens must justify why its bad-state class cannot already be unwritable. Authority is v2.lens.common.construction_justification. This plan is partly superseded: #8141 (2026-08-11) deleted both the #5433 inert-lens backstop and construction-justification presence check. The recorded design is not a live floor guarantee."),
    p(text: "ConstructionClass meanings: WallNow is decidable/grounded construction and raises a home question for a module filed as a lens; WallAfterGrounding is shrinking interim validation with a grounding authority/dissolution mechanism; OutsideModeledGuarantee is the absent-capability column beside the ladder, not a rung or RatchetForever. outside_modeled_guarantee_join.guarantee_boundary_still_outside queries resolve_declaration_ref_live by key over witness_layer_roots: only DeclarationRefDeclarationAbsent means outside; an existing capability invalidates that stamp."),
    p(text: "Class correctness remains human judgment; recording it is mechanically checkable. Each lens carries its own construction_justification declaration, not a parallel ledger. Historical discover_floor_corpus_rows checked that every top-level lens had a discovered fail-closed witness (#5433) and a justification (construction_justification_hygiene_tests). Authoring review cannot substitute for execution, and reachability cannot substitute for justified construction."),
    p(text: "Typed payloads closed the vacuity gap: no rationale/undecidable_because free strings or RatchetForever arm; WallAfterGrounding uses ConstructionMechanism, WallNow uses mechanism plus the shared std.decl_ref.DeclarationRef. wall_now_authority_graph_is_total still checks real declaration targets with a dangling-binding red control. Its host resolver remains a scaffold until a unified kind-agnostic .dag declaration-resolution primitive subsumes it."),
    p(text: "Why the checks were deleted: whole-corpus graph acquisition for a single module’s authorship burdened unrelated witness discovery. Before #8140 all roster consumers paid; demand-directed #8140 removed regen’s cost; #8141 removed both remaining censuses and the inert-lens self-recursive builtin stubs. This was an enforcement regression: missing justification or an unreached lens became writable and undetected by those checks. Historical classification totals are not a maintained invariant; review diligence is strictly weaker."),
    p(text: "Next rung: enforce each module’s authorship facts at ingestion, where that module is already parsed, not in a world-wide witness-roster census. Until execution establishes this, the class remains mitigatable. Preserve typed model, on-module declarations and the independent WallNow graph witness. Class correctness remains review; cost/application_serializer WallNow modules and affected_set_examples support placement remain a separate home/resolution follow-up."),
  ]
}

data construction_justification_rule_plan: Plan = Plan {
  projection: PlanIsAuthorityOnly { ruling: project_documentation_projections_are_not_checkout_artifacts },
  slug: "construction-justification-rule",
  title: "The construction-justification rule (authoring-time) — §0",
  body: construction_justification_rule_body(),
  retirement: PlanRetiresWhen { condition: unbound_dissolution(description: "SUPERSEDED TRIGGER (2026-08-11, gunbc#8141): the original condition named the fail-closed presence check running in discover_floor_corpus_rows, and that check is deleted, so the trigger as written can never fire — an unreachable condition is a lifecycle claim that structurally cannot report itself satisfied. Replacement: delete this doc when the construction-justification requirement is re-established at ingestion — the authorship fact checked where the module is already parsed, one module's facts from one module's source, rather than reconstructed corpus-wide by a consumer that wanted a witness roster — at which point the rule is again a witnessed property and this design doc is redundant. Until then the doc is retained as the record of what was built, why it was deleted, and what the repository currently does NOT enforce.")
  }
}
